  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x,y),$ where\n\n$$\nF(1,1)=0.6,\\,F(1,0)=0.5,\\,F(1,-1)=0.2,\n$$\n\nand the supports of $X$ and $Y$, respectively, are\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\},\\,{S}_{Y}=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le 1,-1<Y\\le 1).$",
